WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.335
-Guys, it is Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.069
when I take care of
some business.

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:05.738
You know,
I get some things done.

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.807
But the day just got
completely away from me.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:12.444
I was busy gathering twigs
for a homemade wreath.

00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:13.913
And I totally forgot to
write out

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.414
my weekly thank-you notes,
right now,

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:16.916
as I was grabbing those twigs.

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.818
You guys mind if I write out

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:19.952
my weekly thank-you notes
right now?

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:21.020
Is that okay? Is that --

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.521
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:24.757
You guys are the best.
Thank you so much.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:25.858
James, can I have some

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:28.627
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:29.863
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:33.999
Thank you, new video game
"Cyberpunk 2077,"

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.669
for letting everyone live out
their wildest fantasy,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.773
walking around
a crowded city without a mask.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.113
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:51.317
Thank you,
Apple's new AirPods Max,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.654
for letting me pay $549
for the privilege of

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:56.455
constantly thinking,
"I'm gonna get mugged,

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:57.590
I'm gonna get mugged,

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.993
I'm gonna get mugged,
I'm gonna get..."

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:07.199
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:09.668
Thank you,
holiday TV commercials,

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:12.038
for teaching us
the true meaning of Christmas,

00:01:12.038 --> 00:01:16.176
wealthy couples buying each
other matching luxury S.U.V.s.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.218
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:28.020
Thank you, Toblerone,
for combining

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.459
my two favorite things, Swiss
chocolate and traffic spikes.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.330
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:41.033
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.069
Thank you, chimney sweeps,
for basically giving

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:46.773
a COVID test to my house.

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:56.416
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.584
Thank you,
Christmas-tree ornaments,

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.854
for making it possible for
Jesus, Rudolph, and Baby Yoda

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:04.457
to all hang out
in my living room.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.229
You get it? "Hang out."

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.598
-Oh, wow.

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.400
Yeah.

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.506
-This next one is
really going to

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.275
knock you out of your loafers.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.743
-Okay.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.711
-Is that what they say?

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.613
-No. Who's -- Who?
Who are "they"?

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:31.250
-Oh, people, uh...boaters.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.553
-Here's one to really
knock you out of your loafers.

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:37.490
-This one will really
knock your socks off.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.559
-The year was 1967.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:44.463
-Sorry. I'm wrong.
It was 1916.

00:02:44.463 --> 00:02:45.498
Alright, here we go.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.166
I think you're gonna
like this one.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:48.768
-Okay.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:51.604
-Actually,
I haven't read it yet.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.839
I don't think you'll like it.

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:54.907
-We're waiting.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.543
-This is our last one,
right here.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.345
-Oh, no.
-But you know what?

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:04.650
We'll be back next Friday
with brand-new thank-you notes.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.985
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.821
Thank you, Pixar, for
announcing that Chris Evans

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.624
will be Buzz Lightyear in
an upcoming film.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:12.991
Makes sense he'd play Buzz,

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.794
since we've already seen
his Woody.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.896
Hey, everybody,
that's our thank-you notes.

